{
	"Set": [
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-08T16:13:50Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1022,
				20
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add Tauri 2.x invoke compatibility across all polyfills\n\nUpdate Tauri invoke calls in all Wind polyfills and services to support both Tauri 1.x and 2.x APIs. The invoke pattern changed from `window.__TAURI__.invoke()` (Tauri 1.x) to `window.__TAURI__.core.invoke()` (Tauri 2.x).\n\nChanges:\n- Update invokeTauri() in: ChildProcessPolyfill, FileProtocolShim, FileSystemPolyfill, IPCRendererShim, NativeModulePolyfill, ProcessPolyfill, SharedProcessProxy\n- Update InvokeMountain() in TauriMainProcessService\n- Add TelemetryLive layer to Bootstrap configuration\n- Reorganize TextModelResolver import in Tauri.ts layer\n\nAll polyfills now check for Tauri 2.x first (core.invoke), then fall back to 1.x patterns, ensuring backward compatibility with existing Tauri 1.x deployments while enabling Tauri 2.x upgrades.",
			"SHA": "14c15166326ad501986bc36dbd49f45458ff6779"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-08T13:01:29Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1022,
				5
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add Tauri-native IPC routing and complete workbench configuration\n\nImplement two parallel IPC pathways to replace Electron's ipcMain:\n\n1. **IPCRendererShim binary protocol loopback**: Re-implement VS Code's binary IPC serialization (SerializeIPC/DeserializeIPC) to handle vscode:message events with loopback responses. Provides stub handlers for channels (logger, storage, configuration, localFilesystem) to prevent workbench hangs.\n\n2. **TauriMainProcessService**: New drop-in replacement for ElectronIPCMainProcessService that routes channel.call() directly through Tauri invoke to Mountain's WindServiceHandlers. Eliminates binary protocol overhead entirely - uses plain JSON over Tauri commands.\n\n3. **ResolveConfiguration**: Extend with full INativeWindowConfiguration including profiles, colorScheme, accessibilitySupport, and other DesktopMain fields. Also fix appRoot to strip origin (workbench prepends vscode-file://), and set VSCODE_DEV: \"true\" for relative imports.\n\nThis enables the VS Code workbench to initialize in the Tauri webview with either protocol path.",
			"SHA": "19bbd809f09ee8f7a5602026ec86e8eccab12a81"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Auto",
			"Date": "2026-04-08T02:40:45Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1020,
				1
			],
			"Message": "",
			"SHA": "d90ebba7a5e23db846de74defc95ec289d321aad"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-07T18:59:49Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1020,
				4
			],
			"Message": "fix(Wind): Enable WKWebView compatibility with relative imports\n\nSet VSCODE_DEV: \"true\" in both Install.ts userEnv and ProcessPolyfill default config. This tells the Electron workbench to use relative imports instead of vscode-file:// URLs, resolving the WKWebView (macOS) limitation where custom URL schemes cannot be used with import().\n\nAlso fix potential null reference in ProcessPolyfill by deferring hrtimeStart initialization. The previous code called process.hrtime() at module evaluation time, but Wind sets window.vscode.process after Install.ts runs, not globalThis.process. Initialize to [0, 0] and let the actual timer start lazily.\n\nThese changes enable the VS Code workbench to render properly in the Tauri webview on macOS.",
			"SHA": "08d44f858d718408383987ee3444fa6495dab051"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-07T18:04:11Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1020,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Extend ResolveConfiguration with complete INativeWindowConfiguration\n\nAdd full Electron workbench configuration to ResolveConfiguration() including:\n- appRoot set to embedded assets path (/Static/Application/)\n- INativeWindowConfiguration fields: mainPid, machineId, sqmId, devDeviceId,\n  isPortable, execPath, homeDir, tmpDir, userDataDir, logLevel, loggers,\n  perfMarks, colorScheme, autoDetectHighContrast, autoDetectColorScheme\n- profiles configuration with default user data paths\n- product metadata (nameShort, nameLong)\n\nThis provides the complete configuration interface that the Electron workbench expects, enabling proper window initialization and workspace setup.",
			"SHA": "d3b21da43c1dae751577ab3080f7e7f56d93b74c"
		}
	],
